androidware: direct-mode prototype - host thunks in Arm user-mode emulation (qemu-arm)

A guest stub ("mov ip, #id; svc 0x9f0100; bx lr") reaches cpu_loop() as the
private syscall 0xf0100 and is dispatched to aw_thunk_call(), which calls the
host's own EGL / OpenGL ES with the guest's AAPCS soft-float arguments; guest
pointers become host pointers, so vertex arrays and textures are not copied.
Function list = what experiments/direct-mode/glbench.c uses. See
docs/direct-mode.md.

--- a/linux-user/arm/cpu_loop.c
